  "url": "hawaii-ws-furtherReflections.html#ex-ws-further-koku",
  "type": "Worksheet Exercise",
  "number": "3.2.9",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Every country has different measuring systems. Did you know that there is a unit of measurement that was used in ancient times and is based on the time it takes to cook rice? Can you guess which culture used this unique method of measuring time and what the unit is called?    The unique unit of measurement based on the time it takes to cook rice comes from ancient Japan. It's called the moment or 刻 (koku) in Japanese. A koku is traditionally defined as the amount of time it takes for an incense stick to burn, which is approximately the same amount of time it takes to cook rice.   "
